Use the graph’s `stream` method with `stream_mode="messages"` and `version="v2"`. The stream yields chunks; when `chunk["type"] == "messages"` the `chunk["data"]` tuple contains a message object whose `content` field is emitted token‑by‑token. You can iterate over the stream and print each token as it arrives. Optionally, filter the tokens by the node name (or tags) in the metadata to limit output to a specific LLM invocation.

```python
for chunk in graph.stream(
 {"topic": "ice cream"},
 stream_mode="messages", # stream LLM tokens
 version="v2",
):
 if chunk["type"] == "messages":
 msg, meta = chunk["data"]
 # optional node filter
 if msg.content and meta["langgraph_node"] == "call_model":
